WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.482
Pandas can run custom Python functions, but custom row-by-row logic is often slower and harder to read than a built-in

00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:17.292
vectorized operation. In the example, margin is calculated by dividing the profit column by the sales column directly.

00:00:17.292 --> 00:00:21.262
That single expression works across the entire table.

00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:25.293
A mapping function is then used only for display formatting.

00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:31.668
When possible, prefer built-in Pandas operations, NumPy operations,

00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:38.268
or vectorized column expressions before writing custom row-wise user-defined functions.

00:00:38.268 --> 00:00:42.279
This usually produces code that is shorter, clearer, and more efficient.

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:51.978
Use custom functions when the problem truly requires logic that cannot be expressed cleanly with built-in operations.
